> [After the] martyrdom of St. Boniface, Ver[g]ilius was made Bishop of Salzburg[ (]766 or 767) and laboured[ successfully] for the upbuilding of his diocese as well as for[ the] spread of[ the] Faith in neighbouring heat[hen] countries, especially in Carinthia. He died at Salzburg, 27 November, 7[89.] In 1233 he[ was] canonized by Gregory IX. His[ doctrine] that[ the] earth is a sphere was derived from the[ teaching] of ancient[ ge]ographers, and his belief in the existence of the antipodes was probably influenced by the accounts which the ancient[ Irish] voyagers gave of[ their] journeys. This, at least, is[ the] opinion of[ R]ettberg ("K[irc]hengesch. Deutschlands", II, 236).

